error[E0401]: `f` is `own`, so it must be used exactly once, but `run_twice` may use it more than once
  --> oneshot.ck:15:14
   |
15 | fn run_twice f -> r : f~own (Unit -> Unit), r~Unit
   |              ^
   = help: `own` promises a single use, so the argument may be a resource; remove `own` if the value must be used twice

error[E0401]: `file` holds a resource (`File`), and a closure that uses it may be called more than once, or never
  --> oneshot.ck:36:9
   |
36 | fn bad1 file -> r : file~File, r~Unit
   |         ^^^^
   = note: a closure using `file` is passed to `many`, whose parameter is not `own`, so `many` may call it any number of times
   = help: mark that parameter of `many` with `own` (as in `f~own (Unit -> a)`)

